===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|Canada|cryptozoology|folklore}} A very large, hairy, [[humanoid]] [[creature]], similar to the [[yeti]], said to live in the [[wilderness]] areas of the [[United States]] and [[Canada]], especially the [[Pacific Northwest]].
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=October 6, 1958
|author=Andrew Genzoli
|title=Huge Foot Prints Hold Mystery Of Friendly Bluff Creek Giant
|journal=w:Humboldt Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20100611030959/https://press.uchicago.edu/Images/Chicago/Buhs_fig12.jpeg
|archivedate=June 11, 2010
|issn=
|oclc=320776427
|page=
|text=This imprint was made either Wednesday night or early Thursday morning by "'''Big Foot'''".
|brackets=on}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=July 1, 1961
|title=Big deal
|journal=Boot and Shoe Recorder
|url=https://archive.org/details/sim_boot-and-shoe-recorder_1961-07-01_160_3/
|volume=160
|issue=3
|location=Philadelphia, Pa.
|publisher=w:Chilton Company
|oclc=1536821
|page=68
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_boot-and-shoe-recorder_1961-07-01_160_3/page/n69/
|column=3
|section=The Last Word
|text=Stories of “'''Bigfoot''',” an eight-foot denizen of the forest in Northern California’s wild Trinity County, are among the main topics of conversation in that area. He is supposedly an Indian or half-breed who has reverted to an animal existence. A footprint believed to be his was measured by a Redding shoe store owner and found to be size 24!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Sun Bear (author)|Sun Bear]]; Wabun Wind; Shawnodese|chapter=A Dream Language of the Earth|title=Dreaming with the Wheel: How to Interpret and Work with your Dreams Using the Medicine Wheel|publisher=Fireside|year=1994|page=145|isbn=0-671-78416-1|passage=Some Earth people believe '''Bigfoot''' lives in underground caves; others believe '''Bigfoot''' is connected with extraterrestrials; still others believe '''Bigfoot''' is a spirit that can sometimes manifest in form.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Bryan Sykes|chapter=The Guru|title=Bigfoot, Yeti, and the Last Neanderthal: A Geneticist’s Search for Modern Apemen|publisher=Disinformation Books|year=2016|section=part II|page=173|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bigfootyetilastn0000syke/page/173/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-938875-15-1|passage=Then there are the sharp divisions of opinion about whether '''Bigfoot''' is a ''Gigantopithecus'' or a Neanderthal or some other hominid.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Christopher D. Bader; Joseph O. Baker|chapter=Bigfoot: Undiscovered Primate or Interdimensional Spirit?|title=Deviance Management: Insiders, Outsiders, Hiders, and Drifters|publisher=w:University of California Press|year=2019|page=77|isbn=9780520304482|passage=Many enthusiasts believe that '''Bigfoot''' is not some sort of undiscovered hominid, but rather a mystical being that moves between dimensions.}}

